solution:
Work in base 100 and use 100 \equiv -3 \pmod{103}. Write 567890123 as blocks: 5|67|89|01|23. Compute iteratively:
- r_0 = 5
- r_1 \equiv r_0\cdot 100 + 67 \equiv 5\cdot(-3) + 67 = -15 + 67 = 52 \pmod{103}
- r_2 \equiv r_1\cdot 100 + 89 \equiv 52\cdot(-3) + 89 = -156 + 89 = -67 \equiv 36 \pmod{103}
- r_3 \equiv r_2\cdot 100 + 1 \equiv 36\cdot(-3) + 1 = -108 + 1 = -107 \equiv 99 \pmod{103}
- r_4 \equiv r_3\cdot 100 + 23 \equiv 99\cdot(-3) + 23 = -297 + 23 = -274 \equiv -274 + 309 = 35 \pmod{103}
Thus n = 35.

Use 100 \equiv 3 \pmod{97} and group as 1|23|45|67|89. Compute iteratively:
- r_0 = 1
- r_1 \equiv r_0\cdot 100 + 23 \equiv 1\cdot 3 + 23 = 26 \pmod{97}
- r_2 \equiv r_1\cdot 100 + 45 \equiv 26\cdot 3 + 45 = 78 + 45 = 123 \equiv 26 \pmod{97}
- r_3 \equiv r_2\cdot 100 + 67 \equiv 26\cdot 3 + 67 = 78 + 67 = 145 \equiv 48 \pmod{97}
- r_4 \equiv r_3\cdot 100 + 89 \equiv 48\cdot 3 + 89 = 144 + 89 = 233 \equiv 233 - 194 = 39 \pmod{97}
Therefore n = 39.

Use 100 \equiv 11 \pmod{89} and group by pairs: 20|23|20|23|20|23. Compute:
- r_0 = 20
- r_1 \equiv r_0\cdot 100 + 23 \equiv 20\cdot 11 + 23 = 243 \equiv 243 - 178 = 65 \pmod{89}
- r_2 \equiv r_1\cdot 100 + 20 \equiv 65\cdot 11 + 20 = 735 \equiv 735 - 712 = 23 \pmod{89}
- r_3 \equiv r_2\cdot 100 + 23 \equiv 23\cdot 11 + 23 = 276 \equiv 276 - 178 = 98 \equiv 9 \pmod{89}
- r_4 \equiv r_3\cdot 100 + 20 \equiv 9\cdot 11 + 20 = 119 \equiv 119 - 89 = 30 \pmod{89}
- r_5 \equiv r_4\cdot 100 + 23 \equiv 30\cdot 11 + 23 = 353 \equiv 353 - 267 = 86 \pmod{89}
Thus r = 86.

