With $a_1=x$, $a_2=31$, and recurrence $a_{n+1} = \dfrac{a_n+1}{a_{n-1}}$, the first five terms are
$a_1=x$, $a_2=31$, $a_3=\dfrac{32}{x}$, $a_4=\dfrac{x+32}{31x}$, $a_5=\dfrac{x+1}{31}$, and $a_6=x$ (5-periodic).
Setting 32 equal to one of $\{a_1,a_3,a_4,a_5\}$ gives four solutions:
- $x=32$;
- $\dfrac{32}{x}=32 \Rightarrow x=1$;
- $\dfrac{x+32}{31x} = 32 \Rightarrow x = \dfrac{32}{31\cdot 32 - 1} = \dfrac{32}{991}$;
- $\dfrac{x+1}{31} = 32 \Rightarrow x = 31\cdot 32 - 1 = 991$.
The product of these four values is $32 \cdot 1 \cdot \dfrac{32}{991} \cdot 991 = 32^2 = 1024$.
